(753424, 79665, 5112, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  I thought yours was better than mine, I wanted to take mine down after seeing yours.  The seeds are so sharp, and the background so smooth.  I like this very much.<br/> <br/>Ursula<br/> <br/>PS - I''d been wondering all week whose shot this was :))<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-07 12:54:09.</i></td>', 'Congratulations!  I thought yours was better than mine, I wanted to take mine down after seeing yours.  The seeds are so sharp, and the background so smooth.  I like this very much. Ursula PS - I''d been wondering all week whose shot this was :))', '2004-06-07 13:53:28.000000', '2004-06-07 13:54:09.000000', 0),
(753439, 80174, 714, '<td valign="top">Thanks folks for the kind comments.  This was by far the hardest shot I have ever taken.  These critters move fast.  5th place isn''t to bad. :-)</td>', 'Thanks folks for the kind comments.  This was by far the hardest shot I have ever taken.  These critters move fast.  5th place isn''t to bad. :-)', '2004-06-07 14:05:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(753514, 79707, 8054, '<td valign="top">This is interesting, I swear I wrote a comment last night but I guess I forgot to click on "Post" when I was done.<br/> <br/>As you can see from my comments above, I did take this in the late afternoon around 5:30. The sun was setting and it cast a nice orange/red light. I compared both color, slightly desturated and b/w images before I decided on b/w. I felt it had more impact as a modified contrast b/w than if it had any color.<br/> <br/>As far as showing more of the dock area, if I did that then you would see the other dock numbers and the ground which was not interesting. In fact, I even played with the idea of showing even less of the dock door and only the numbers but then some folks might not know what the partial dock door was so I showed it all.<br/> <br/>Doors #1 and #3 are not visible because #1 is out of frame completely and the support pillar blocks #3. I guess you had to be very creative and imagine the other doors there instead of me showing all 3 of them.<br/> <br/>Thanks to those who left comments for me!</td>', 'This is interesting, I swear I wrote a comment last night but I guess I forgot to click on "Post" when I was done. As you can see from my comments above, I did take this in the late afternoon around 5:30. The sun was setting and it cast a nice orange/red light. I compared both color, slightly desturated and b/w images before I decided on b/w. I felt it had more impact as a modified contrast b/w than if it had any color. As far as showing more of the dock area, if I did that then you would see the other dock numbers and the ground which was not interesting. In fact, I even played with the idea of showing even less of the dock door and only the numbers but then some folks might not know what the partial dock door was so I showed it all. Doors #1 and #3 are not visible because #1 is out of frame completely and the support pillar blocks #3. I guess you had to be very creative and imagine the other doors there instead of me showing all 3 of them. Thanks to those who left comments for me!', '2004-06-07 15:04:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(753524, 80121, 8054, '<td valign="top">How did I miss voting on this one? I know I didn''t get to all of them but I''m sure I would have recognized this one. Great job with the desat and soft focus. And the slight vignetting is also a very nice touch as it adds to the emotion of the ballerinas. Great job!</td>', 'How did I miss voting on this one? I know I didn''t get to all of them but I''m sure I would have recognized this one. Great job with the desat and soft focus. And the slight vignetting is also a very nice touch as it adds to the emotion of the ballerinas. Great job!', '2004-06-07 15:12:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(753586, 80122, 18644, '<td valign="top">If this one ever become a print, i''m buying one :)</td>', 'If this one ever become a print, i''m buying one :)', '2004-06-07 15:58:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(753625, 79548, 21611, '<td valign="top">I am very new to photography so take my comments accordingly!!!  The clarity is very good. I spent a good deal of time looking at the head of the plant. The detail is exceptional. I guess that in a competition like this B&amp;W pics probably start off 1 to 2 points lower than where they should be. I am sure that some color would have placed you very near the top. I know you have done that in the past and I think it would have worked here as well. I do think its a great gallery shot and will try in the future not to be prejudiced against B&amp;W pics. I think your work is inspiring.</td>', 'I am very new to photography so take my comments accordingly!!!  The clarity is very good. I spent a good deal of time looking at the head of the plant. The detail is exceptional. I guess that in a competition like this B&W pics probably start off 1 to 2 points lower than where they should be. I am sure that some color would have placed you very near the top. I know you have done that in the past and I think it would have worked here as well. I do think its a great gallery shot and will try in the future not to be prejudiced against B&W pics. I think your work is inspiring.', '2004-06-07 16:31:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(753695, 80122, 11897, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BruB:</b></div><hr/><i> If this one ever become a print, i''m buying one :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You might regret saying that Martin, I''ve uploaded one and am awaiting approval :)<br/>Thanks a bunch for the compliment, I won''t hold you to it.<br/>Paul.</td>', 'Originally posted by BruB: If this one ever become a print, i''m buying one :)   You might regret saying that Martin, I''ve uploaded one and am awaiting approval :)Thanks a bunch for the compliment, I won''t hold you to it.Paul.', '2004-06-07 17:18:36.000000', NULL, 0),
