(755811, 80274, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Overall the image is very strong, well composed, there is a richness to the tonal values you chose to present.  There really isn''t anything I would change to the image itself but I would lose the blueish gray in the border, just doesn''t do anything for it.  Seems to be more of a distraction than a help.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', 'Critique Club Overall the image is very strong, well composed, there is a richness to the tonal values you chose to present.  There really isn''t anything I would change to the image itself but I would lose the blueish gray in the border, just doesn''t do anything for it.  Seems to be more of a distraction than a help. Anna', '2004-06-08 23:38:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(755812, 80189, 10818, '<td valign="top">I gave it an 7, then after looking at it more, I gave it an 8.  The guys head sticking out the window, the steam, and the sheep made it for me.  The only thing I might have done is chop it a bit tighter on the right.  Nice shot.</td>', 'I gave it an 7, then after looking at it more, I gave it an 8.  The guys head sticking out the window, the steam, and the sheep made it for me.  The only thing I might have done is chop it a bit tighter on the right.  Nice shot.', '2004-06-08 23:38:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(755891, 80121, 200, '<td valign="top">It is hard for me to explain how i did this as I am more intuitive than technical. I sit around and play with things until I get a desired result or trash it. Results are experimental. I layerd the image first and adjusted levels...erasing to the original layer in areas that needed it. Flattened the image and layered again...adding a bit of blur to soften the dreadful background and erasing parts to expose the dancers...adjusted levels on both layers. Flattened and layered again to desaturate and erase areas to bring out color...again adjusting levels on both layers. I finished it with a bit of diffuse glow to soften and lighten it further. I saw a lot of flaw in this but went with it anyway...I had given up on the experiment and settled with what i had. I still thought it was pretty. :)</td>', 'It is hard for me to explain how i did this as I am more intuitive than technical. I sit around and play with things until I get a desired result or trash it. Results are experimental. I layerd the image first and adjusted levels...erasing to the original layer in areas that needed it. Flattened the image and layered again...adding a bit of blur to soften the dreadful background and erasing parts to expose the dancers...adjusted levels on both layers. Flattened and layered again to desaturate and erase areas to bring out color...again adjusting levels on both layers. I finished it with a bit of diffuse glow to soften and lighten it further. I saw a lot of flaw in this but went with it anyway...I had given up on the experiment and settled with what i had. I still thought it was pretty. :)', '2004-06-09 00:53:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(755961, 80215, 8816, '<td valign="top">if you wanted to get rid of the reflections in the glasses what you could do is take the same picture against a white background, lighting only with a light aimed from below the table at the white background.  Then you could invert the picture, leaving you with a similar picture to what you have now, without the nasty reflections.  An excellent shot though, i love playing with glass, your concept here is very similar to my ''ornate'' shot.</td>', 'if you wanted to get rid of the reflections in the glasses what you could do is take the same picture against a white background, lighting only with a light aimed from below the table at the white background.  Then you could invert the picture, leaving you with a similar picture to what you have now, without the nasty reflections.  An excellent shot though, i love playing with glass, your concept here is very similar to my ''ornate'' shot.', '2004-06-09 01:17:54.000000', NULL, 0),
